guide polestar-experimental/shendralas
title Shen'dralas (experimental)
levels 42-44
zone Shen'dralas
coords live
folder Shen'dralas · Experimental
why Forever's new zone south of Desolace, an alpha route written from players' recordings.
keywords shen'dralas, shendralas, valley of bones, evenshade's overlook, forlorn gardens, bristleback retreat, pylons, desolace, experimental, alpha
next forever/horde/40-50/04-tanaris
next forever/alliance/40-50/03-feralas
pitch A detour south of Desolace into Shen'dralas: 11 quests around a fallen Highborne temple, for levels 41-45.
pro About 27,500 quest experience plus the kills
pro Brings you back to the main route where you left it
pro Its experience comes off the grinding the route asks for before level 50: about an hour sooner to 60
con Its quests are about on level at 43 and a few levels under you at 46
con Elites walk the Valley of Bones: Corpsefeeders and Magram Necrokhans, level 45
con Experimental: written from a handful of players' recordings

# Polestar Experimental, Shen'dralas for both factions (2026-11-12). Hand-written from players' recordings of
# the zone (99 sessions, 56 people, most of them passing through below level 40), with Forever's quest data for
# titles, levels and objectives and the client's tables for item and spell names. A detour for levels 41-45,
# offered as a route choice. Horde: offered at the end of the Feralas, Dustwallow Marsh & Swamp of Sorrows guide
# (40-50/03, Camp Mojache, about level 46); in from Shadowprey Village, out by hearth to Camp Mojache, where the
# Tanaris guide picks up at the flight master. Alliance: offered at the end of the Badlands guide (40-50/02,
# Theramore, about level 43); in from Nijel's Point, out on the ride south into Feralas, where the Feralas guide
# picks up at the Feathermoon boat.
# Order: the Tattered Journal from the valley's necromancers; Mordent Evenshade's pylons (find the three, the
# fragment and the shard in Desolace's two centaur villages, the Mana Sieve and the repairs, his story, then
# Magister Kirandis in the temple); the temple's own quests once Kirandis has been met; Mithera's Forlorn Gardens.
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (players' recordings, one player each, so leads to confirm):
# Fragments of the Pylons after Strange Pylons; Powering the Pylons after Fragments of the Pylons; A Brief History
# Lesson after Powering the Pylons; Meeting the Magister after A Brief History Lesson; What They've Done to My
# Peonies and Word of the Woods after Forlorn Gardens. Mithera was only recorded after Meeting the Magister was
# handed in, so the temple's quests wait for it here.
# Left out on purpose:
# - The Gelkis and Magram quests of the Valley of Bones (Nerlokh, Orgrul, Hagiak, Rokren; Valley of Bones,
#   Khan Jehn and the rest): each asks for Honored with its centaur clan (forever/reputation/centaur-clans).
# - Vindael's Phantasmal Problems (93450), Spectral Iron Ore (93546) and Tempered Expectations (96060): nobody
#   recorded them, and the data places none of the spectral ore deposits.
# - Mana Mania (99258): its Nascent Pylon Protector is an elite (level 43), and nobody recorded it.
# - Rot and Regret (93404, Maraudon), Passing the Blame (93601) after it, Agamaggan's Blood (93604, Razorfen Downs)
#   and Not on Squealing Terms (93606): dungeon quests and their follow-ups; Kog'thug the Brave, who gives the last
#   two, was hostile to every player who met him.
# - Corpsefeeder's Carapace (93574, from an elite) and Forlorn Necklace (93609, no known source).

step Fly to Shadowprey Village
  only Horde
  when !zone "Shen'dralas"
  when !zone "Desolace"
  tip Experimental route (alpha). It follows what players did in Shen'dralas and may still have rough spots: if a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip Shen'dralas lies south of Desolace, through the Valley of Bones, and has no flight path of its own. Its quests are for levels 41-45. Coming from the Eastern Kingdoms, take the zeppelin to Orgrimmar first (from Grom'gol or the Undercity).
  fly "Shadowprey Village"

step Fly to Nijel's Point
  only Alliance
  when !zone "Shen'dralas"
  when !zone "Desolace"
  tip Experimental route (alpha). It follows what players did in Shen'dralas and may still have rough spots: if a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip Shen'dralas lies south of Desolace, through the Valley of Bones, and has no flight path of its own. Its quests are for levels 41-45. Coming from the Eastern Kingdoms, take the boat from Menethil Harbor to Theramore first.
  fly "Nijel's Point"

step Into the Valley of Bones
  only Horde
  when !zone "Shen'dralas"
  zone Shen'dralas
  tip Ride east from Shadowprey Village along Desolace's southern edge, past Gelkis Village: the Valley of Bones opens there into Shen'dralas.
  enter "Shen'dralas" @21.2,22.4

step Into the Valley of Bones
  only Alliance
  when !zone "Shen'dralas"
  zone Shen'dralas
  tip Ride south from Nijel's Point down the road through eastern Desolace to Magram Village: just past its western edge the path climbs into the Valley of Bones and Shen'dralas.
  enter "Shen'dralas" @33.0,5.8

step The Valley of Bones: a Tattered Journal
  zone Shen'dralas
  tip Experimental route (alpha): if a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip The Outcast Necromancers and the Magram Necromancers of the valley drop a Tattered Journal whose writer lives in Shen'dralas: players got it within a few kills. The Magram centaurs leave you be until you attack; the Magram Necrokhans among them (level 45) are elites: leave them be.
  collect 260347
  accept 93644

step The western pylon
  tip East through the valley to the strange crystal on its pedestal: clicking it starts Strange Pylons. The Decrepit Pylon Protectors (levels 42-43) around it are the mana elementals that guard it. Corpsefeeders (level 45, elite) roam the valley east of here.
  accept 92914 object 577959

step Bristleback Retreat: the eastern pylon
  tip East along the valley road to the quilboar of Bristleback Retreat: the second pylon stands at the eastern end of their camp. A Corpsefeeder (level 45, elite) walks this road: let it pass. The Bristlebacks (levels 42-43) attack on sight; Kog'thug the Brave (level 43, elite) and his bodyguards hold the south side of the camp.
  goto 73.2,23.2 "the eastern pylon" r 15

step The temple of Shen'dralas: the third pylon
  tip South to the Shen'dralar temple at the zone's heart, keeping west of Kog'thug's bodyguards: the third pylon stands inside. The temple's guards are neutral: leave them be.
  complete 92914 @47.6,76.7

step Evenshade's Overlook
  tip North-west from the temple to Mordent Evenshade's camp on the overlook, beside the spirit healer: the Tattered Journal is his, and he wants to hear about the pylons.
  turnin 93644
  turnin 92914
  accept 96010

step North into Desolace
  zone Desolace
  tip Mordent wants a fragment and a shard of the pylons back from Desolace's two centaur villages: Magram Village lies just beyond the valley's northern way out.
  enter "Desolace" @64.0,80.4

step Magram Village
  zone Desolace
  tip The Pylon Fragment lies at the western edge of the village; Magram Guardians (levels 39-41) watch over it.
  collect 255656 x1 quest 96010.1 @68.1,79.2

step Gelkis Village
  zone Desolace
  tip West along Desolace's southern edge to Gelkis Village: the Pylon Shard lies at its southern end, watched by Gelkis Guardians (levels 39-41).
  collect 255657 x1 quest 96010.2 @36.1,85.6

step Back into the Valley of Bones
  zone Shen'dralas
  tip East again along Desolace's southern edge: the Valley of Bones opens into Shen'dralas.
  enter "Shen'dralas" @21.2,22.4

step Evenshade's Overlook
  turnin 96010
  accept 96018

step The temple: the Mana Sieve
  tip Mordent sends you for the Mana Sieve, kept inside the temple beside Historian Biraxas. Powering the Pylons asks you to gather mana with the Sieve before you repair the pylons: with it in your bags you can handle the Unstable Mana Rifts, the floating sparks of mana all along the road north.
  collect 255662 @45.9,78.2
  accept 99257 optional               -- Historian Biraxas, if he offers it: a Decrepit Pylon Protector's heart, from the road north and the pylons

step The western pylon: repair it
  tip North up the road to the first pylon, gathering mana from the Unstable Mana Rifts on the way. Then repair the pylon with the Pile of Pylon Parts (Repair and Recharge Pylon). Decrepit Pylon Protectors guard it.
  use 271882 quest 96018.2 @43.97,35.59 -- Pile of Pylon Parts: Repair and Recharge Pylon
  collect 286647 quest 99257.1 optional -- Depleted Crystal Heart, from the Decrepit Pylon Protectors

step Bristleback Retreat: repair the eastern pylon
  tip East along the valley road to the eastern pylon and repair it the same way, coming in from the west: Kog'thug the Brave (level 43, elite) and his bodyguards hold the south side of the quilboar camp, and a Corpsefeeder (level 45, elite) walks the road.
  use 271882 quest 96018.3 @73.4,23.91 -- Pile of Pylon Parts: Repair and Recharge Pylon
  collect 286647 quest 99257.1        -- Depleted Crystal Heart, from the Decrepit Pylon Protectors at either pylon

step Evenshade's Overlook
  tip Back west along the valley road and south to Mordent. A Brief History Lesson asks you to hear him out: talk to him once more, then hand it in.
  turnin 96018
  accept 93016
  talk 253471 quest 93016.1           -- Mordent Evenshade: hear him out
  turnin 93016
  accept 93394

step Liranne
  when has 259461
  tip A Prowler gave up a Partially Digested Collar: Liranne, north of the temple, knows whose it was.
  accept 93568
  turnin 93568

step The temple: Magister Kirandis
  tip Magister Kirandis waits inside the temple. Then Mithera, on the temple's eastern side, has work in the Forlorn Gardens.
  turnin 93394
  turnin 99257                        -- Historian Biraxas, if you took it and carry the heart
  accept 93341

step The Forlorn Gardens: the pedestal
  tip East of the temple the Forlorn Gardens have run wild, and their plants attack on sight. Examine the pedestal at the gardens' southern end.
  complete 93341 @70.3,79.7

step Mithera
  turnin 93341
  accept 93362
  accept 93594

step The Forlorn Gardens
  tip Rowdy Roses and Terrible Tulips grow all over the gardens; the Malevolent Marigolds keep to the northern part. Woodwyrd, the treant in the middle of the gardens, has a request of his own that needs water from Maraudon, a dungeon: this guide leaves it.
  kill 254566 x4 quest 93362.1        -- Rowdy Rose
  kill 254567 x4 quest 93362.2        -- Terrible Tulip
  kill 254572 x20 quest 93362.3       -- Malevolent Marigold
  turnin 93594

step Mithera
  tip Historian Biraxas, inside the temple, may have a task for you if you didn't take it earlier: the heart of a Decrepit Pylon Protector, a short ride back up the road north. Otherwise Shen'dralas is done: hearth, or ride back north through the Valley of Bones to Desolace's flight points (Shadowprey Village for the Horde, Nijel's Point for the Alliance).
  turnin 93362
  accept 99257 optional               -- Historian Biraxas

step A Heart of Crystal
  tip The nearest Decrepit Pylon Protectors stand by the road north, from the middle of the zone up to the western pylon, and around Mordent's overlook: one of them carries the heart Biraxas wants.
  collect 286647 quest 99257.1

step Historian Biraxas
  tip Shen'dralas is done: hearth, or ride back north through the Valley of Bones to Desolace.
  turnin 99257

step Back to your route
  only Horde
  note Shen'dralas is done. Your Tanaris guide picks up at Camp Mojache's flight master: hearth there, or ride back north through the Valley of Bones to Shadowprey Village and fly to Camp Mojache.

step Back to your route
  only Alliance
  note Shen'dralas is done. Your Feralas guide picks up from here: ride back north through the Valley of Bones, west along Desolace's southern edge and south into Feralas, to the dock on the Forgotten Coast where the boat crosses to Feathermoon Stronghold.
